---
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MetricsDashboard from '../../components/MetricsDashboard.jsx';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.metrics;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath}
  ogType={meta.ogType}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <ContentCard as="section">
<h2>Structural diagnostics</h2>
    <p>These reports describe historical graph counts, route checks, and calculated structural scores. Their scope is the published graph release process.</p>
    <ul><li><strong>Structural coverage:</strong> representation of configured domains and question stages.</li><li><strong>Routing:</strong> configured branch and traversal checks.</li><li><strong>Robustness:</strong> reachability under simulated graph perturbations.</li><li><strong>Historical gates:</strong> results against the thresholds used for the corresponding release.</li></ul>
    <p>These measures describe graph structure rather than investigation effectiveness or Core record conformance. Current question revisions and evidence criteria are documented in the <a href="/graphs/coverage/">coverage ledger</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/graphs/">Graph atlas</a> · <a href="/conformance/">Core validation</a> · <a href="/docs/">All resources</a></p>
  </ContentCard>

  <MetricsDashboard client:load />
</BaseLayout>
